{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/107232-lunar-kuei-jin","id":107232,"title":"Lunar Kuei-Jin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-06T20:55:18-07:00","id":107232,"title":"Lunar Kuei-Jin?","content":"So, I recently picked up a few Dharma books for Kindred of the East at the used book store and, while flipping through them, it's made me wonder about some things. I know that it's never been a secret that KoE was the most Exalted of the old WoD books, but, IIrc, 3e Lunars are going to be those with glorious god-bodies and an inner beast.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if they're going to be similar in nature to the Kuei-Jin to some degree. Obviously they won't be dead or need to feed on the blood of the living, but that struggle to come to terms with the dark side of your personality seems like it might come into play here. <br /> <br /> I dunno. Either way could be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> ....Also, did anyone else notice that Melissa Uran tended to draw really long legs on the Kuei-Jin, especially the women? Is there a story behind that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:05:02-07:00","id":107234,"title":"","content":"Crazy anime style was really en vogue back when those came out.<br /> <br /> I'm uh, not exactly a big fan of KotE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:12:39-07:00","id":107239,"title":"","content":"Lunar Kuei-Jin ? But I thought Infernal was the one with Shintai and Heretical charms !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:20:27-07:00","id":107244,"title":"","content":"The Asian-monster-themed shapeshifting powers in Kuei-Jin would probably fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:36:51-07:00","id":107248,"title":"","content":"Just remember, if you want to use it, you have to make sure that you make it clear that you are a superior being to that 'other' Exalted type, that's clearly inferior to you, and that you don't crush underfoot merely because it might take more than a few months to complete.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Seriously, according to their core book and entire line, they should be able to roll over every Cainite on the planet in about three months. Fucking middle-low Dharma Kuei-jin going into Europe to murder 500+ year-old Cainites, and they basically give it a tiny section, with a not that they basically do it on a lark...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T22:09:14-07:00","id":107255,"title":"","content":"What's interesting is that the KotE served as the basis for the inspiration of the Dragon Blooded. I'm sure that there's a bit you can mine for Lunars there, but I don't think that the writers will draw on them too much when making Lunars.<br /> <br /> And no Nocte, Kuei-jin aren't that badass, and while the Kuei-jin had a high opinion of themselves, the books didn't exactly play it up from an out-of-game perspective. It was pretty clear that the only reason they managed to gain such a strong foothold in California was that they hit the Anarch Free State, and the Anarchs actively refused assistance from the Camarilla even though they were in the middle of a two front war with the Sabbat and the Kuei-jin. If they had tried hitting Camarilla or Sabbat territory they wouldn't have lasted very long.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T22:25:47-07:00","id":107260,"title":"","content":"Nah dude, the Storyteller companion has a section in it where it talks about young Kuei-jin egging each other on to go to Europe, the heart of the Camarilla. While there, they enjoy activities like... showing up unannounced at the courts of Princes, and getting off scot-free, and picking out a random elder, murdering them, and watching the fallout. This is basically to get street cred with other Kuei-jin.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Cainite can't poke their head into pretty much any part of Asia, no matter how powerful they are, and expect to last more than a few <i>days, </i>unless they stay in specifically prescribed territory or have huge bribes. It's very asinine.<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 115. It does note that it's more dangerous than the Kuei-jin really let on, but it also makes it clear that it apparently happens on a semi-regular basis. This is the same chapter that paints ALL OF ASIA as a deathtrap to Cainites, no matter how powerful they are or how many of them come.<br /> <br /> It literally brushes them off as a non-issue. It's terrible writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":374,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","user":"Nocte ex Mortis","date":". 04-07-2014, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T22:30:53-07:00","id":107261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/107232-lunar-kuei-jin#post107232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I recently picked up a few Dharma books for Kindred of the East at the used book store and, while flipping through them, it's made me wonder about some things. I know that it's never been a secret that KoE was the most Exalted of the old WoD books, but, IIrc, 3e Lunars are going to be those with glorious god-bodies and an inner beast.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if they're going to be similar in nature to the Kuei-Jin to some degree. Obviously they won't be dead or need to feed on the blood of the living, but that struggle to come to terms with the dark side of your personality seems like it might come into play here.<br /> <br /> I dunno. Either way could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff from KoTE got used as inspiration before and we ended up with 1e DBT. Use sparingly. That said, I did use some references to KotE in my fourth iteration Moon and Machine Charm conversion, but it actually had more to do with the reaction of the Beast Courts to being tricked into fighting each other by the then-Wan Xian, which was to call to heaven for retribution. This turned the Wan Xian into the Wan Gui, and took from them their living breath.<br /> <br /> So I used the Alchemical &quot;You are now a Void creature&quot; submodule to provide a home for Breath-Drinking Executioner Attack, which under that writeup turns Dragon-Blooded into creatures of death until they can ritually purify themselves. If you squint, there's kind of a parallel between the War of Shame and the Usurpation. You'll have to squint an awful lot, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....Also, did anyone else notice that Melissa Uran tended to draw really long legs on the Kuei-Jin, especially the women? Is there a story behind that? </div> </div> </div>Her style is influenced by Masami Obari. You might remember him from... almost any video game property licensed into an anime in the 90s, such as Fatal Fury and Voltage Fighter Gowcaizer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T23:07:15-07:00","id":107264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/107232-lunar-kuei-jin?p=107260#post107260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah dude, the Storyteller companion has a section in it where it talks about young Kuei-jin egging each other on to go to Europe, the heart of the Camarilla. While there, they enjoy activities like... showing up unannounced at the courts of Princes, and getting off scot-free, and picking out a random elder, murdering them, and watching the fallout. This is basically to get street cred with other Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 95 of Shadow War points out that this is basically a long-term trick by the Prince of Berlin. After he utterly Dominated a group of Kuei-jin he sent them back to Asia with stories about how easy it is to show up in Europe and kill older Vampires and throw everything into chaos there. And those Kuei-jin help send other dumb, young turks into the Prince's clutches who also get turned into puppets and sent back to Asia and so on and so forth... the Prince is getting a fairly powerful gathering of younger Kuei-jin together and under his thumb, though what he has in mind is never explored in later books. <br /> <br /> I can agree that there was bad writing in KotE. There was bad writing in every White Wolf book and line. I don't think its quite as bad as some people make out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T23:41:15-07:00","id":107273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/107232-lunar-kuei-jin#post107232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously they won't be dead or need to feed on the blood of the living, but that struggle to come to terms with the dark side of your personality seems like it might come into play here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cat is out of the bad: In 3e, Lunars *will* need to feed on the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T02:29:59-07:00","id":107341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/107232-lunar-kuei-jin#post107232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Also, did anyone else notice that Melissa Uran tended to draw really long legs on the Kuei-Jin, especially the women? Is there a story behind that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she was just bad at drawing legs. (And other things.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:10:28-07:00","id":116619,"title":"","content":"I read up on the Kuei-Jin fairly recently.<br /> I liked that they emerged from hell as feral monsters that the others needed to track down and teach to act like a person again, it had the potential to be cool back-story element. The closest thing we have to that in Exalted is the Dragon Kings, who don't make as much use of it as they could. I think it's because they're portrayed as really animalistic even after achieving enlightenment which undermines the idea that they clawed their way up from being a beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}